    "abstract": "Parts figure for the vacuum toilet bowl interface, showing the partition bracket and latch in both standards, the interface seal and the harness retention behind the shroud.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure shows the vacuum toilet assembly at the bowl to shroud interface, with the partition bracket, the latch and the harness retention behind the shroud.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows one lavatory looking forward with the shroud removed. Items 10 and 10A are the partition bracket standards; the bracket at item 10 carries the seal groove and must be used with the low force latch. The cable tie at item 30 is the current standard and replaces the earlier tie wherever the harness is disturbed, on any bracket standard."
    },
